nd attention, but communication issues may be problematic. Or we could ask for more info about B's cooperation. But we can also propose that Candidate C might be a stronger alternative due to decision quality and attention, despite communication concerns. However we need to be concise.\n\nGiven the guidelines, we should make a focused argumentative contribution: maybe we can say we see Candidate C as a strong alternative because of quick correct decisions and excellent attention, which are critical for long-distance flights, and his concern for others suggests good crew cooperation, but his communication difficulty and egocentric attitude are concerns. Compare with B.\n\nThus we can say: I think Candidate C may be a stronger overall fit than B because decision quality and attention are paramount, and his concern for others suggests crew cooperation, whereas B's pretentiousness and tone issues may be more severe. However we need to ask for more info on C's communication.\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: \"Can make correct decisions quickly\", \"excellent attention skills\", \"puts concern for others above everything\", \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"regarded as egocentric\", \"not very willing to further his education\". Use these.\n\nWe also need to state our current vote. Could be Candidate C. Or we could keep B but ask for more info. The guidelines: we should not just ask for info; we need to make an argument. We can say we still support B but want to compare with C. Might be better to propose C as alternative.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate C.\n\nWe need to include METADATA_JSON with vote.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: mention Agent 1's recommendation, note B's strengths, but argue C's strengths may outweigh B's concerns. Provide evidence. Conclude with provisional recommendation for C.\n\nLet's craft."}
